    [BugFix][Model][v0.30.0] Fix Engram history and lookup timing in model runner v2 (#18052)
    
    ### What this PR does / why we need it?
    
    Backport #17794 to `releases/v0.30.0`.
    
    Fix DeepSeek V4.1 Engram history and lookup timing in model runner v2.
    Defer fallback lookup until the forward context is available, retain
    graph-captured producers and replay metadata cleanup, and preserve FULL
    graph bucket event identity.
    
    The release base is ac1b7bceb370265e8f794f38d32a88041b0c51c9, which is
    also the base of #17794. All three commits were cherry-picked without
    conflicts; the resulting source tree is identical to #17794 at
    ba7c85870a2ce2fdea5e175342cae46506ec6773.
    
    ### Does this PR introduce _any_ user-facing change?
    
    Correct MRV2 Engram execution; no new configuration options.
    
    ### How was this patch tested?
    
    - 194 related CPU regression tests passed on the release backport,
    covering Engram model state, hooks, registered-model contracts,
    multistream lookup, model runner v2 and graph metadata/replay.
    - `bash format.sh ci` and `git diff --check` passed.
    - Tests used the release branch's verified vLLM pin
    `ced6857afa0ea7b2e3f0846a62e1394e90f15607`.
    - NPU runtime, GPQA accuracy and performance were not rerun for this
    backport. Previous results in #17794 are historical evidence.
    
    - vLLM main:
    https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm/commit/ced6857afa0ea7b2e3f0846a62e1394e90f15607
    
